# Runtime, memory and correctness fixes

Stall follow-up: [measured causes and diagnostic prototypes](RUNTIME_STALL_INVESTIGATION_2026_10_26.md). This later investigation does not ship further runtime changes or close the remaining performance targets.

26 October 2026. Scope: R1-R4, M1-M4 and C1-C5 in [the concrete work list](RUNTIME_MEMORY_CORRECTNESS_TASKS_2026_10_26.md). The fixes below are implemented and checked on desktop. **R3 still falls short of consistently responsive loading frames; M4 still needs static-memory drift attribution and Android acceptance.** These are open acceptance items, not a 10/10 certification.

## Changes

- **R1–R2:** preserve lazy startup, seven cached carousel photographs and one interactive Garage. PNG reads/decoding, encoding/writing and cache-directory trimming now run on one owned worker. Native capture/readback and texture publication stay on the main/render thread. Every result carries its appearance key and weak view reference. Parked Garage explicitly retires its temporary renderer even when its processing is disabled; hidden and superseded results cannot publish. Corrupt-file fallback is exercised.
- **R3:** trace actual App entry for Star and all five current Storm tracks. Whole-world packing/instantiation was only a few milliseconds, so it remains intact. A separate cold **2.21-second canonical gate-layout bake inside restart** now runs in the existing ground worker, using the unchanged `TrackSession._configure` algorithm/cache. Measured restart drops to **13-19 ms**. Stock-car assembly, details, lamp surfaces and batching now yield cooperatively behind an explicit model-ready barrier; synchronous Garage/Profile consumers retain their existing behavior. First use of actual geometry/material combinations is staged under the loading cover with temporary cull margins restored afterward. Cancellation closes its loading state and retires the abandoned Game, including during model details and batching. Winter's immutable road-snow lookup now has an 8 MiB cache, preserving exact cached texture identity and releasing under pressure. Remaining CPU/graphics stalls are quantified below.
- **R4:** unchanged paused frames skip surface/bridge/water/contact queries, car/prop updates and HUD reconstruction. Ambience, audio state and camera settling continue. State, viewport, camera settings and locale invalidate the frozen presentation. Pausing clears shake; resuming clears held controls without advancing canonical time.
- **M1:** live recording is `PackedInt64Array`, with **1,728,000 payload bytes for 216,000 inputs**. Signed steering, all pedal channels, handbrake and launch markers retain exact decoding. Legacy nested arrays remain supported at the persistence/diagnostic boundary. Rewind offsets remain monotonic.
- **M2:** tickets contain small metadata and an owned completed-evidence reference. Proof/ghost containers are sealed once; row traversal and full ghost normalization run on the save worker. The Game can restart or be freed without mutating the queued snapshot. Maximum-size queue handoff measured **0.103 ms** and ghost snapshot **0.056 ms**, excluding later worker serialization. Concurrent claimed-lap metadata is preserved.
- **M3:** pending evidence has a **160 MiB conservative allowance**, including a **96 MiB reservation for encoding and a bounded in-flight wire packet**, a 40 MiB maximum finished packet, existing job/frame limits and reservation before another competitive attempt. Backend CPU encoding/compression jobs share one worker lane. Uploads release redundant decoded proof before network waits. Failed storage retains its owned result and recovery action. Challenge/Rivalry/retry admission happens before reserving a server try; ordinary offline driving remains available.
- **M4:** account for retained Garage meshes, viewport surfaces, decoded card textures, preview IO headroom and optional part/paint images. Keep Garage's 96 MiB allowance separate from the existing 64 MiB editor allowance. Pressure frees hidden Garage, optional image caches and winter lookup data; in-flight saves remain owned by the save service.
- **C1:** restore `assets/news/vehicles/forklift.png` through the established native vehicle-photo baker. Fresh import/export inventory verifies all seven vehicle photographs and their compiled textures. No generated external art or new licence is involved.
- **C2–C3:** atomically write an owner/origin/ticket/key/options/hash manifest before the replay payload. Recovery completes interrupted payload/marker/job commits, including a complete payload temporary file, and never replaces accepted/retry state. Fully committed retries retain their original key and payload bytes. Missing-payload manifests remain uncommitted; they are never acknowledged as saved. Old input-only, old proof-bearing and count/proof/ghost journals retain their established recovery paths.
- **C4–C5:** correct a freed-Game call after the loading draw wait and cancellation cleanup during staged rendering. Modernize obsolete recording signatures and the fixture's handling snapshot, preserving its restart/offline assertions. Keep the existing node-owned pause-row callback. Canonical physics/configuration, route validators and gameplay cameras are unchanged by this task.
- **Recording-limit completion:** finished practice or over-limit evidence clears its unusable competitive ticket, previous challenge outcome and pending challenge seed. The result shows why it cannot enter online standings; Continue can leave the race. It claims a local save only when that save succeeded. Valid recordings with temporary storage failures retain their original ticket and recovery action. The actual App test covers duplicate completion callbacks and old outcome cleanup.

